:: t0_day03_evening_transition [home]
<<run SOY.Time.ensureSlot(2)>>
<<run SOY.Locations.travel('street')>>
<<scene "mood/october-evening-walk-2" "Ninth Street after dark, amber sodium light, a woman ahead with keys between her fingers">>

The facility door closes behind me and I'm back on Ninth Street and the cold hits my face like a correction. Like the world saying: you're back, this is real air, real October, real noise.

I stand on the sidewalk for a moment. Hands in my jacket pockets. The olive green jacket with the torn lining. My body feels, I keep coming back to this word but it's the only one that fits, specific. Angular where Katya was curved. Flat where she was full. My hands are too big. My stride is too wide. When I walked in her body, the hips dictated the gait, the sway wasn't a choice, it was architecture. Now my hips are narrow and my legs swing forward like pendulums and the gait is efficient, purposeful, completely without music.

The bus stop is right there. I could go home. Chipi is waiting. The couch is waiting. The Modelo in the fridge is waiting.

I don't want quiet. Not tonight. After the mirror and the shower and the knock, after Katya's body blushed without my permission and her heart rate spiked when the actor knocked on the door, I need noise. I need a room full of people who have never had their consciousness extracted and compressed and installed in someone else's nervous system. I need the specific banality of a bar where people are drunk and arguing about soccer and nobody is thinking about what it means to inhabit a stranger's skin.

My body is doing that thing again. The phantom sway. Walking down the sidewalk in my own boots with my own narrow hips and my gait keeps trying to adjust, the brain sending instructions calibrated for a pelvis that's no longer there. Flor's echo was subtle. Katya's is louder. Two transfers now, two different female bodies, and my motor cortex is starting to treat the sway as a setting instead of an anomaly. Like it's building a library. Male gait. Female gait. Toggle.

I pass a woman walking her dog. Small terrier, rhinestone collar, the woman in a puffy jacket and yoga pants. She walks with her keys threaded between her fingers, the jagged edges poking outward like improvised brass knuckles. I notice because I wouldn't have noticed a week ago. Before Flor. Before Katya. Before the knock on the door and the way the body froze in its vulnerability and my first instinct was to cover up and protect modesty I didn't own.

The woman glances at me as I pass. Quick assessment. Threat evaluation. A calculation performed in less than a second, processed and discarded, the keys staying between her fingers regardless. She's not afraid of me specifically. She's afraid of the category I belong to. Male. Night. Sidewalk. Alone.

I want to tell her she's right to be cautious. I also want to tell her I understand now, or at least I'm starting to, what it costs to walk through the world with that calculation running in the background every single time.

I don't tell her anything. I keep walking. She keeps walking. The dog sniffs a fire hydrant.

<<opt "choice_day03_evening" "Decide where the night goes">>


:: choice_day03_evening [home]
<<if SOY.Body.hasPhantoms()>>
The phantom sway is still there. Hip memory from a body I left an hour ago. My gait keeps adjusting for a pelvis that isn't there.
<</if>>

I could go home. Chipi. The couch. A beer. Quiet.

But quiet is the last thing I need tonight.

<<opt "t0_day03_vega_enter" "Head to Vega" "A bar Paco's taken me to twice. Latin music. Cheap mezcal. Noise, and the bartender he keeps mentioning.">>
<<opt "t0_day03_lulu_stop" "Stop at Lulu's bodega" "Milk for tomorrow's coffee. An empanada. Life advice I didn't ask for.">>
<<opt "t0_day03_evening_walk" "Walk the neighborhood" "Cold air. Room to think. Nowhere in particular.">>
<<opt "t0_day03_evening_home_direct" "Go straight home" "Chipi. Beer. Processing.">>


:: t0_day03_evening_walk [home]
<<run SOY.Locations.travel('street')>>

I walk. No destination. Down Ninth, across, back up a block I don't usually take. The cold is honest. It asks nothing of me except that I keep moving, and moving is the one thing my body knows how to do without a committee vote.

The phantom sway rides along. Two transfers deep and my motor cortex keeps offering me Katya's gait like a helpful assistant suggesting the wrong file. I let it. There's no one to see me overcorrect on an empty street at seven-thirty on a Wednesday.

A couple argues quietly outside a laundromat, the fight of people who've had it before and know all the moves. A man in an apron drags a bag of trash to the curb and nods at me the way strangers nod when it's cold and late enough that being outside together counts as something. The amber streetlights turn every puddle into a small held photograph.

By the time my feet decide I'm done, I've walked a loop and I'm four blocks from home with nothing solved and my head a little quieter. Which is all a walk is ever for.

<<opt "t0_day03_evening_home_direct" "Home">>


:: t0_day03_evening_home_direct [home]
<<run SOY.Locations.travel('apartment')>>
<<scene "mood/apartment-night-couch" "The apartment, one lamp, the cat in a nest of dish towel on the counter">>
<<if not visited("t0_day03_lulu_stop") and not visited("t0_day03_vega_enter")>>
<<run SOY.Economy.spend(2, 'food')>>
<</if>>

Home. Chipi is on the kitchen counter sitting in the exact center of a dish towel she pulled off the oven handle and arranged into a nest. She looks at me like I interrupted something important.

I feed her. Open a Modelo. Sit on the couch. The apartment is quiet. Not the bad quiet from the first weeks after the layoff. A different kind. Processing quiet. The quiet of a mind working through too much data with too few categories.

<<opt "t0_day03_phone_evening" "Check the phone">>


:: t0_day03_phone_evening [phone]
<<set _lyla = visited("t0_day03_phone_lyla")>>
<<set _james = visited("t0_day03_phone_james")>>
<<set _paco = visited("t0_day03_phone_paco")>>

<<if visited("t0_day03_phone_evening") lte 1>>
The phone has been buzzing in my pocket for the last hour.
<<else>>
The phone again.
<</if>>

<<if not _lyla>>
<<phone "Lyla">>
<<txt "Lyla">>Wednesday check-in. Are you alive?<</txt>>
<</phone>>
<<opt "t0_day03_phone_lyla" "Answer Lyla" "She has theories. Four of them.">>
<</if>>

<<if not _james>>
<<phone "James">>
<<txt "James">>Hey Manuel. Quick question, still on for tomorrow night? I'm excited about the Thai place. Also I told my mom about your new job and she says congratulations and also she wants to know if you eat enough.<</txt>>
<</phone>>
<<opt "t0_day03_phone_james" "Answer James" "Thursday. 7 PM. His treat, don't argue.">>
<</if>>

<<if not _paco and not visited("t0_day03_vega_adriana")>>
<<phone "Paco">>
<<txt "Paco">>Day 3 report. When you're home. I want EVERYTHING.<</txt>>
<</phone>>
<<opt "t0_day03_phone_paco" "Call Paco" "He'll want the ethics module and the bartender, in that order of stated priority and reverse order of actual interest.">>
<<elseif not _paco>>
<<opt "t0_day03_phone_paco" "Call Paco" "Tell him about Vega before Lulu does.">>
<</if>>

<<opt "t0_day03_night_processing" "Put the phone down. Bed.">>
<<if $settings.showExplicit and not visited("t0_day03_solo_night")>>
<<opt "t0_day03_solo_night" "Put the phone down. Then pick it back up." "Explicit. Processing what the transfer left in the body.">>
<</if>>


:: t0_day03_night_processing [home intimate]
<<run SOY.Quests.complete('t0_day03', 'wind_down')>>
<<scene "mood/bed-night" "The bedroom at 11 PM: amber blind-lines across the bed, one hand on a flat chest, the cat at the hip">>

Shower. Hot water. Steam.

<<if $settings.showExplicit>>
I stand under the spray and press both palms flat against my chest. Flat. The pectorals are there, firm, ordinary. No weight. No softness. No give. Katya's body had breasts that shifted when she, when I, unbuttoned the shirt. The bra held them in place like a structure, an architecture of wire and fabric, and when the training top came off and I felt them move inside the bra, the body blushed. I didn't tell it to blush. It just did. Heat rising from the collarbones to the cheeks in a wave I couldn't control.

My own face doesn't blush. I don't think it's ever blushed. Mexican skin, thick enough to keep the blood from advertising itself.
<<else>>
I stand under the spray with both hands flat on my chest. Flat, ordinary, no weight to it. Katya's body did not feel like this. I turn the water hotter and let the thought dissolve in the steam.
<</if>>

I turn off the water. Dry off. Boxers. The bed.

Chipi arrives within thirty seconds of my head hitting the pillow. She curls against my hip, her purr a low mechanical thrum that vibrates through the mattress.

The dark settles. This is usually when the processing starts, the body lying still while the mind replays the day's impossible footage. Flor yesterday. Katya today. The mirror. Four seconds. Auburn hair and pale skin and the curve of breasts under a grey training top and my brain short-circuiting between "that's me" and "that's not me" and some third option that doesn't have language yet.

I roll onto my side. My body, this body, responds with familiar inputs. The weight of my own arm on my ribcage. My hip digging into the mattress. The specific way my legs stack, ankles knocking.

<<if $settings.showExplicit>>
But underneath, lower, there's warmth. Not an erection. Not yet. More diffuse. The phantom echo of Katya's body running through my nervous system like a song stuck in my head, except instead of melody it's sensation. The blush. The temperature response. The moment the actor knocked and my, her, heart rate spiked and something tightened in the lower belly that I don't have the equipment to reproduce but my brain is trying anyway.

I don't act on it. Not tonight. The warmth sits there, unfocused, and I let it sit. I'm too tired to decode it and too honest to pretend it isn't there.

My hand moves to my hip. The bone juts under the skin, sharp, angular, a shelf of pelvis that holds nothing up. Katya's hips were wider. The bone sat deeper, padded by muscle and fat in a way that made sitting feel different, lying feel different, everything below the waist constructed on a broader foundation. My pelvis is narrow. Utilitarian. Built for forward motion, not for the lateral sway that Katya's body insisted on.

I press my thumb into the hip bone. Hard surface under thin skin. Mine.
<<else>>
The transfer echoes follow me to bed. Katya's body left fingerprints in my nervous system that my own body tries to read and can't quite translate. I lie in the dark, full of data I don't have categories for, and I don't reach for any of it. Not tonight.
<</if>>

Both bodies are specific now. Both have a shape and a weight and a way of lying in a bed. My body used to be the default. The only option. The unmarked category. After two days of inhabiting female architecture, my maleness has become a marked category too. A thing with qualities instead of just a thing.

I don't know what to do with that. I file it with the rest of the undecoded data. The drawer is getting full.

In the living room, Chipi knocks something off a shelf. The sound is small, plastic, probably the pen I left on the bookcase. I hear her paws hit the floor afterward, the satisfied thump of a cat who has completed her mission.

<<say "Me">>Buenas noches, Chipi.<</say>>

She purrs from somewhere in the dark. I close my eyes. The afterimage of a mirror with the wrong face in it floats behind my eyelids for a moment, then fades.

<<opt "t0_day03_sleep" "Let sleep show up">>


:: t0_day03_sleep
<<if $calendar.day is 3>>
	<<run SOY.Time.ensureSlot(3)>>
	<<run SOY.Time.advance()>>
	<<run SOY.Body.decayPhantoms()>>
<</if>>
<<run SOY.Locations.travel('apartment')>>

Sleep comes eventually. Not peacefully. More like it shows up and insists.

<<opt "t0_day04_wake" "Day 4">>
